From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd939x: treat a failed zdet ramp as floating impedance

wcd939x_mbhc_get_result_params() leaves *zdet untouched on a ramp error.
The caller starts zdet at 0 and reuses the same variable for the right
channel, so a failed left ramp reads as 0 ohm and a failed right ramp
inherits the left channel's value. Either way the headphone can be
classified as mono. Report a floating impedance instead, as the ramp's
own "no load" result does.

The same fix as for wcd938x (0845).
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
index 010d12466..8dbd47fca 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -2068,6 +2068,7 @@ static void wcd939x_mbhc_get_result_params(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 		dev_dbg(component->dev,
 			"%s: Impedance detect ramp error, c1=%d, x1=0x%x\n",
 			__func__, c1, x1);
+		*zdet = WCD939X_ZDET_FLOATING_IMPEDANCE;
 		goto ramp_down;
 	}
 
